#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus IBM gratis tentang informasi dan komputasi kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simon's algorithm"
msgstr "Algoritma Simon"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore Leftrightarrow */}\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore Leftrightarrow */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Simon's algorithm is a quantum query algorithm for a problem known as *Simon's problem*.\n"
"This is a promise problem with a flavor similar to the Deutsch-Jozsa and Bernstein-Vazirani problems, but the specifics are different.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Simon adalah algoritma kueri kuantum untuk masalah yang dikenal sebagai *masalah Simon*.\n"
"Ini adalah masalah janji dengan nuansa serupa masalah Deutsch-Jozsa dan Bernstein-Vazirani, tetapi spesifikasinya berbeda.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Simon's algorithm is significant because it provides an *exponential* "
"advantage of quantum over classical (including probabilistic) algorithms, "
"and the technique it uses inspired Peter Shor's discovery of an efficient "
"quantum algorithm for integer factorization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Simon penting karena memberikan keunggulan *eksponensial* kuantum "
"atas algoritma klasik (termasuk probabilistik), dan teknik yang digunakannya"
" menginspirasi penemuan Peter Shor tentang algoritma kuantum efisien untuk "
"faktorisasi bilangan bulat.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Simon's problem {#simons-problem}"
msgstr "Masalah Simon {#simons-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The input function for Simon's problem takes the form\n"
msgstr "Fungsi input untuk masalah Simon berbentuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma^m\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma^m\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for positive integers $n$ and $m.$\n"
"We could restrict our attention to the case $m = n$ in the interest of simplicity, but there's little to be gained in making this assumption — Simon's algorithm and its analysis are basically the same either way.\n"
msgstr ""
"untuk bilangan bulat positif $n$ dan $m.$\n"
"Kita bisa membatasi perhatian pada kasus $m = n$ demi kesederhanaan, tetapi tidak banyak yang didapat dari membuat asumsi ini — algoritma Simon dan analisisnya pada dasarnya sama dengan cara manapun.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Simon's problem\">\n"
"Input: a function $f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma^m$ \\\n"
"Promise: there exists a string $s\\in\\Sigma^n$ such that $[f(x) = f(y)] \\Leftrightarrow\n"
"[(x = y) \\vee (x \\oplus s = y)]$ for all $x,y\\in\\Sigma^n$ \\\n"
"Output: the string $s$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Masalah Simon\">\n"
"Input: fungsi $f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma^m$ \\\n"
"Janji: ada string $s\\in\\Sigma^n$ sedemikian sehingga $[f(x) = f(y)] \\Leftrightarrow\n"
"[(x = y) \\vee (x \\oplus s = y)]$ untuk semua $x,y\\in\\Sigma^n$ \\\n"
"Output: string $s$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll unpack the promise to better understand what it says momentarily, but first let's be clear that it requires that $f$ has a very special structure — so most functions won't satisfy this promise.\n"
"It's also fitting to acknowledge that this problem isn't intended to have practical importance.\n"
"Rather, it's a somewhat artificial problem tailor-made to be easy for quantum computers and hard for classical computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan mengurai janjinya untuk lebih memahami apa yang dikatakannya sebentar lagi, tetapi pertama-tama mari kita perjelas bahwa itu mengharuskan $f$ memiliki struktur yang sangat khusus — sehingga sebagian besar fungsi tidak akan memenuhi janji ini.\n"
"Juga tepat untuk mengakui bahwa masalah ini tidak dimaksudkan untuk memiliki kepentingan praktis.\n"
"Sebaliknya, ini adalah masalah agak buatan yang sengaja dibuat mudah untuk komputer kuantum dan sulit untuk komputer klasik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are two main cases: the first case is that $s$ is the all-zero string "
"$0^n,$ and the second case is that $s$ is not the all-zero string.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ada dua kasus utama: kasus pertama adalah bahwa $s$ adalah string semua-nol "
"$0^n,$ dan kasus kedua adalah $s$ bukan string semua-nol.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Case 1: $s=0^n.$\n"
"If $s$ is the all-zero string, then we can simplify the if and only if statement in the promise so that it reads $[f(x) = f(y)] \\Leftrightarrow [x = y].$\n"
"This is equivalent to $f$ being a one-to-one function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kasus 1: $s=0^n.$\n"
"Jika $s$ adalah string semua-nol, kita bisa menyederhanakan pernyataan jika-dan-hanya-jika dalam janji sehingga berbunyi $[f(x) = f(y)] \\Leftrightarrow [x = y].$\n"
"Ini setara dengan $f$ sebagai fungsi satu-ke-satu.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Case 2: $s\\neq 0^n.$\n"
"If $s$ is not the all-zero string, then the promise being satisfied for this string implies that $f$ is *two-to-one*, meaning that for every possible output string of $f,$ there are exactly two input strings that cause $f$ to output that string. Moreover, these two input strings must take the form $w$ and $w \\oplus s$ for some string $w.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kasus 2: $s\\neq 0^n.$\n"
"Jika $s$ bukan string semua-nol, maka janji yang dipenuhi untuk string ini menyiratkan bahwa $f$ adalah *dua-ke-satu*, artinya untuk setiap string keluaran yang mungkin dari $f,$ ada tepat dua string masukan yang menyebabkan $f$ mengeluarkan string itu. Selain itu, dua string masukan ini harus berbentuk $w$ dan $w \\oplus s$ untuk beberapa string $w.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It's important to recognize that there can only be one string $s$ that works"
" if the promise is met, so there's always a unique correct answer for "
"functions that satisfy the promise.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penting untuk disadari bahwa hanya ada satu string $s$ yang bisa cocok jika "
"janji dipenuhi, sehingga selalu ada jawaban yang unik dan benar untuk fungsi"
" yang memenuhi janji.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's an example of a function taking the form $f:\\Sigma^3 \\rightarrow "
"\\Sigma^5$ that satisfies the promise for the string $s = 011.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut adalah contoh fungsi berbentuk $f:\\Sigma^3 \\rightarrow \\Sigma^5$ "
"yang memenuhi janji untuk string $s = 011.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"f(000) & = 10011 \\\\\n"
"f(001) & = 00101 \\\\\n"
"f(010) & = 00101 \\\\\n"
"f(011) & = 10011 \\\\\n"
"f(100) & = 11010 \\\\\n"
"f(101) & = 00001 \\\\\n"
"f(110) & = 00001 \\\\\n"
"f(111) & = 11010\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"f(000) & = 10011 \\\\\n"
"f(001) & = 00101 \\\\\n"
"f(010) & = 00101 \\\\\n"
"f(011) & = 10011 \\\\\n"
"f(100) & = 11010 \\\\\n"
"f(101) & = 00001 \\\\\n"
"f(110) & = 00001 \\\\\n"
"f(111) & = 11010\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are $8$ different input strings and $4$ different output strings, each of which occurs twice — so this is a two-to-one function.\n"
"Moreover, for any two different input strings that produce the same output string, we see that the bitwise XOR of these two input strings is equal to $011,$ which is equivalent to saying that either one of them equals the other XORed with $s.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ada $8$ string masukan yang berbeda dan $4$ string keluaran yang berbeda, masing-masing terjadi dua kali — jadi ini adalah fungsi dua-ke-satu.\n"
"Selain itu, untuk dua string masukan yang berbeda yang menghasilkan string keluaran yang sama, kita melihat bahwa XOR bitwise dari dua string masukan ini sama dengan $011,$ yang setara dengan mengatakan bahwa salah satunya sama dengan yang lain yang di-XOR dengan $s.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that the only thing that matters about the actual output strings is whether they're the same or different for different choices of input strings.\n"
"For instance, in the example above, there are four strings $(10011,$ $00101,$ $00001,$ and $11010)$ that appear as outputs of $f.$ We could replace these four strings with different strings, so long as they're all distinct, and the correct solution $s = 011$ would not change.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa satu-satunya hal yang penting tentang string keluaran yang sebenarnya adalah apakah mereka sama atau berbeda untuk pilihan string masukan yang berbeda.\n"
"Misalnya, dalam contoh di atas, ada empat string $(10011,$ $00101,$ $00001,$ dan $11010)$ yang muncul sebagai keluaran $f.$ Kita bisa mengganti empat string ini dengan string yang berbeda, selama semuanya berbeda, dan solusi yang benar $s = 011$ tidak akan berubah.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Algorithm description {#algorithm-description}"
msgstr "Deskripsi algoritma {#algorithm-description}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here's a quantum circuit diagram representing Simon's algorithm.\n"
msgstr "Berikut adalah diagram sirkuit kuantum yang mewakili algoritma Simon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Simon's algorithm](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-"
"algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Simon.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Algoritma Simon](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-"
"algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Simon.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be clear, there are $n$ qubits on the top that are acted upon by Hadamard gates and $m$ qubits on the bottom that go directly into the query gate.\n"
"It looks very similar to the algorithms we've already discussed in the lesson, but this time there's no phase kickback; the bottom $m$ qubits all go into the query gate in the state $\\vert 0\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk lebih jelasnya, ada $n$ qubit di atas yang dikenai gate Hadamard dan $m$ qubit di bawah yang langsung masuk ke gate kueri.\n"
"Tampilannya sangat mirip dengan algoritma yang sudah kita bahas dalam pelajaran, tetapi kali ini tidak ada phase kickback; semua $m$ qubit bawah masuk ke gate kueri dalam keadaan $\\vert 0\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To solve Simon's problem using this circuit will actually require several "
"independent runs of it followed by a classical post-processing step, which "
"will be described later after the behavior of the circuit is analyzed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk memecahkan masalah Simon menggunakan sirkuit ini sebenarnya memerlukan"
" beberapa jalankan independen diikuti oleh langkah pemrosesan pasca-klasik, "
"yang akan dijelaskan nanti setelah perilaku sirkuit dianalisis.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Analysis {#analysis}"
msgstr "Analisis {#analysis}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The analysis of Simon's algorithm begins along similar lines to the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm.\n"
"After the first layer of Hadamard gates is performed on the top $n$ qubits, the state becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"Analisis algoritma Simon dimulai dengan cara yang sama dengan algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa.\n"
"Setelah lapisan pertama gate Hadamard dilakukan pada $n$ qubit atas, keadaannya menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} \\vert 0^m \\rangle \\vert x\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} \\vert 0^m \\rangle \\vert x\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When the $U_f$ is performed, the output of the function $f$ is XORed onto "
"the all-zero state of the bottom $m$ qubits, so the state becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"Ketika $U_f$ dilakukan, keluaran fungsi $f$ di-XOR ke keadaan semua-nol dari"
" $m$ qubit bawah, sehingga keadaannya menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} \\vert f(x) \\rangle \\vert x\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} \\vert f(x) \\rangle \\vert x\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When the second layer of Hadamard gates is performed, we obtain the "
"following state by using the same formula for the action of a layer of "
"Hadamard gates as before.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ketika lapisan kedua gate Hadamard dilakukan, kita mendapatkan keadaan "
"berikut menggunakan rumus yang sama untuk aksi lapisan gate Hadamard seperti"
" sebelumnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y\\in\\Sigma^n} (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\vert f(x) \\rangle \\vert y\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y\\in\\Sigma^n} (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\vert f(x) \\rangle \\vert y\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point, the analysis diverges from the ones for the previous "
"algorithms in this lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada titik ini, analisis menyimpang dari analisis untuk algoritma-algoritma "
"sebelumnya dalam pelajaran ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We're interested in the probability for the measurements to result in each possible string $y\\in\\Sigma^n.$\n"
"Through the rules for analyzing measurements described in the *Multiple systems* lesson of the *Basics of quantum information* course, we find that the probability $p(y)$ to obtain the string $y$ is equal to\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita tertarik pada probabilitas pengukuran menghasilkan setiap string yang mungkin $y\\in\\Sigma^n.$\n"
"Melalui aturan untuk menganalisis pengukuran yang dijelaskan dalam pelajaran *Beberapa sistem* dari kursus *Dasar-dasar informasi kuantum*, kita menemukan bahwa probabilitas $p(y)$ untuk mendapatkan string $y$ sama dengan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p(y) = \\left\\|\\frac{1}{2^n} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\vert f(x) \\rangle \\right\\|^2.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p(y) = \\left\\|\\frac{1}{2^n} \\sum_{x\\in\\Sigma^n} (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\vert f(x) \\rangle \\right\\|^2.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To get a better handle on these probabilities, we'll need just a bit more notation and terminology.\n"
"First, the *range* of the function $f$ is the set containing all of its output strings.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk lebih memahami probabilitas ini, kita memerlukan sedikit lebih banyak notasi dan terminologi.\n"
"Pertama, *jangkauan* dari fungsi $f$ adalah himpunan yang berisi semua string keluarannya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{range}(f) = \\{ f(x) : x\\in \\Sigma^n \\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{range}(f) = \\{ f(x) : x\\in \\Sigma^n \\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Second, for each string $z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f),$ we can express the "
"set of all input strings that cause the function to evaluate to this output "
"string $z$ as $f^{-1}(\\{z\\}).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kedua, untuk setiap string $z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f),$ kita dapat "
"menyatakan himpunan semua string masukan yang menyebabkan fungsi "
"mengevaluasi ke string keluaran $z$ ini sebagai $f^{-1}(\\{z\\}).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"f^{-1}(\\{z\\}) = \\{ x\\in\\Sigma^n : f(x) = z \\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"f^{-1}(\\{z\\}) = \\{ x\\in\\Sigma^n : f(x) = z \\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The set $f^{-1}(\\{z\\})$ is known as the *preimage* of $\\{z\\}$ under $f.$\n"
"We can define the preimage under $f$ of any set in place of $\\{z\\}$ in an analogous way — it's the set of all elements that $f$ maps to that set.\n"
"(This notation should not be confused with the *inverse* of the function $f,$ which may not exist.\n"
"The fact that the argument on the left-hand side is the set $\\{z\\}$ rather than the element $z$ is the clue that allows us to avoid this confusion.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Himpunan $f^{-1}(\\{z\\})$ dikenal sebagai *preimage* dari $\\{z\\}$ di bawah $f.$\n"
"Kita bisa mendefinisikan preimage di bawah $f$ dari himpunan manapun sebagai pengganti $\\{z\\}$ dengan cara yang analog — itu adalah himpunan semua elemen yang dipetakan $f$ ke himpunan tersebut.\n"
"(Notasi ini tidak boleh dikacaukan dengan *invers* dari fungsi $f,$ yang mungkin tidak ada.\n"
"Fakta bahwa argumen di sisi kiri adalah himpunan $\\{z\\}$ bukan elemen $z$ adalah petunjuk yang memungkinkan kita menghindari kebingungan ini.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using this notation, we can split up the sum in our expression for the probabilities above\n"
"to obtain\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan notasi ini, kita bisa memisahkan jumlahan dalam ekspresi kita untuk probabilitas di atas\n"
"untuk mendapatkan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p(y) =\n"
"\\left\\|\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f)}\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})}  (-1)^{x\\cdot y}\\Biggr)\n"
"\\vert z \\rangle\n"
"\\right\\|^2.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p(y) =\n"
"\\left\\|\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f)}\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})}  (-1)^{x\\cdot y}\\Biggr)\n"
"\\vert z \\rangle\n"
"\\right\\|^2.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ is represented exactly once by the two "
"summations — we're basically just putting these strings into separate "
"buckets depending on which output string $z = f(x)$ they produce when we "
"evaluate the function $f,$ and then summing separately over all the "
"buckets.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ direpresentasikan tepat sekali oleh dua "
"penjumlahan — kita pada dasarnya hanya menempatkan string-string ini ke "
"dalam ember terpisah tergantung pada string keluaran mana $z = f(x)$ yang "
"mereka hasilkan saat kita mengevaluasi fungsi $f,$ kemudian menjumlahkan "
"secara terpisah atas semua ember.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can now evaluate the Euclidean norm squared to obtain\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita sekarang bisa mengevaluasi kuadrat norma Euclidean untuk mendapatkan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p(y) = \\frac{1}{2^{2n}}\n"
"\\sum_{z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f)}\n"
"\\left\\vert \\sum_{x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})}  (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\right\\vert^2.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p(y) = \\frac{1}{2^{2n}}\n"
"\\sum_{z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f)}\n"
"\\left\\vert \\sum_{x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})}  (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\right\\vert^2.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To simplify these probabilities further, let's take a look at the value\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menyederhanakan probabilitas ini lebih lanjut, mari kita lihat nilai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\left\\vert \\sum_{x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})}  (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\right\\vert^2\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\left\\vert \\sum_{x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})}  (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\right\\vert^2\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for an arbitrary selection of $z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f).$\n"
msgstr "untuk pilihan arbitrer dari $z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If it happens to be the case that $s = 0^n,$ then $f$ is a one-to-one function and there's always just a single element $x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\}),$ for every $z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f).$\n"
"The value of the expression $(1)$ is $1$ in this case.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika ternyata $s = 0^n,$ maka $f$ adalah fungsi satu-ke-satu dan selalu ada hanya satu elemen $x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\}),$ untuk setiap $z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f).$\n"
"Nilai ekspresi $(1)$ adalah $1$ dalam kasus ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If, on the other hand, $s\\neq 0^n,$ then there are exactly two strings in the set $f^{-1}(\\{z\\}).$\n"
"To be precise, if we choose $w\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})$ to be any one of these two strings, then the other string must be\n"
"$w \\oplus s$ by the promise in Simon's problem.\n"
"Using this observation we can simplify $(1)$ as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika, di sisi lain, $s\\neq 0^n,$ maka ada tepat dua string dalam himpunan $f^{-1}(\\{z\\}).$\n"
"Lebih tepatnya, jika kita memilih $w\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})$ sebagai salah satu dari dua string ini, maka string lainnya harus\n"
"$w \\oplus s$ berdasarkan janji dalam masalah Simon.\n"
"Menggunakan observasi ini kita bisa menyederhanakan $(1)$ sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\left\\vert \\sum_{x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})}  (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\right\\vert^2\n"
"& = \\Bigl\\vert (-1)^{w\\cdot y} + (-1)^{(w\\oplus s)\\cdot y} \\Bigr\\vert^2 \\\\\n"
"& = \\Bigl\\vert (-1)^{w\\cdot y} \\Bigl(1 + (-1)^{s\\cdot y}\\Bigr) \\Bigr\\vert^2 \\\\\n"
"& = \\Bigl\\vert 1 + (-1)^{y\\cdot s} \\Bigr\\vert^2 \\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{cases}\n"
"4 & y \\cdot s = 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & y \\cdot s = 1\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\left\\vert \\sum_{x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})}  (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\right\\vert^2\n"
"& = \\Bigl\\vert (-1)^{w\\cdot y} + (-1)^{(w\\oplus s)\\cdot y} \\Bigr\\vert^2 \\\\\n"
"& = \\Bigl\\vert (-1)^{w\\cdot y} \\Bigl(1 + (-1)^{s\\cdot y}\\Bigr) \\Bigr\\vert^2 \\\\\n"
"& = \\Bigl\\vert 1 + (-1)^{y\\cdot s} \\Bigr\\vert^2 \\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{cases}\n"
"4 & y \\cdot s = 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & y \\cdot s = 1\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, it turns out that the value $(1)$ is independent of the specific choice "
"of $z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f)$ in both cases.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi, ternyata nilai $(1)$ tidak bergantung pada pilihan spesifik "
"$z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f)$ dalam kedua kasus.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can now finish off the analysis by looking at the same two cases as "
"before separately.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita sekarang bisa menyelesaikan analisis dengan melihat dua kasus yang sama"
" seperti sebelumnya secara terpisah.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Case 1: $s = 0^n.$ In this case the function $f$ is one-to-one, so there are"
" $2^n$ strings $z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f),$ and we obtain\n"
msgstr ""
"Kasus 1: $s = 0^n.$ Dalam kasus ini fungsi $f$ adalah satu-ke-satu, sehingga"
" ada $2^n$ string $z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f),$ dan kita mendapatkan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  p(y) = \\frac{1}{2^{2n}} \\cdot 2^n = \\frac{1}{2^n}.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  p(y) = \\frac{1}{2^{2n}} \\cdot 2^n = \\frac{1}{2^n}.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  In words, the measurements result in a string $y\\in\\Sigma^n$ chosen "
"uniformly at random.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Dengan kata lain, pengukuran menghasilkan string $y\\in\\Sigma^n$ yang "
"dipilih secara seragam acak.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Case 2: $s \\neq 0^n.$\n"
"In this case $f$ is two-to-one, so there are $2^{n-1}$ elements in $\\operatorname{range}(f).$\n"
"Using the formula from above we conclude that the probability to measure each $y\\in\\Sigma^n$ is\n"
msgstr ""
"Kasus 2: $s \\neq 0^n.$\n"
"Dalam kasus ini $f$ adalah dua-ke-satu, sehingga ada $2^{n-1}$ elemen dalam $\\operatorname{range}(f).$\n"
"Menggunakan rumus dari atas kita menyimpulkan bahwa probabilitas mengukur setiap $y\\in\\Sigma^n$ adalah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  p(y)\n"
"  = \\frac{1}{2^{2n}} \\sum_{z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f)}\n"
"  \\Biggl\\vert \\sum_{x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})} (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\Biggr\\vert^2\n"
"  =\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2^{n-1}} & y \\cdot s = 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  0 & y \\cdot s = 1\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  p(y)\n"
"  = \\frac{1}{2^{2n}} \\sum_{z\\in\\operatorname{range}(f)}\n"
"  \\Biggl\\vert \\sum_{x\\in f^{-1}(\\{z\\})} (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\Biggr\\vert^2\n"
"  =\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2^{n-1}} & y \\cdot s = 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  0 & y \\cdot s = 1\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  In words, we obtain a string chosen uniformly at random from the set $\\{y\\in\\Sigma^n : y \\cdot s = 0\\},$ which\n"
"  contains $2^{n-1}$ strings. (Because $s\\neq 0^n,$ exactly half of the binary strings of length $n$ have binary dot\n"
"  product $1$ with $s$ and the other have binary dot product $0$ with $s,$ as we already observed in the analysis of\n"
"  the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm for the Bernstein-Vazirani problem.)\n"
msgstr ""
"  Dengan kata lain, kita mendapatkan string yang dipilih secara seragam acak dari himpunan $\\{y\\in\\Sigma^n : y \\cdot s = 0\\},$ yang\n"
"  berisi $2^{n-1}$ string. (Karena $s\\neq 0^n,$ tepat setengah dari string biner dengan panjang $n$ memiliki hasil kali titik biner $1$ dengan $s$ dan yang lain memiliki hasil kali titik biner $0$ dengan $s,$ seperti yang sudah kita amati dalam analisis algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa untuk masalah Bernstein-Vazirani.)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Classical post-processing {#classical-post-processing}"
msgstr "Pemrosesan pasca-klasik {#classical-post-processing}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now know what the probabilities are for the possible measurement outcomes when we run the quantum circuit for Simon's algorithm.\n"
"Is this enough information to determine $s$?\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita sekarang tahu apa probabilitas untuk kemungkinan hasil pengukuran ketika kita menjalankan sirkuit kuantum untuk algoritma Simon.\n"
"Apakah ini cukup informasi untuk menentukan $s$?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The answer is yes, provided that we're willing to repeat the process several times and accept that it could fail with some probability, which we can make very small by running the circuit enough times.\n"
"The essential idea is that each execution of the circuit provides us with statistical evidence concerning $s,$ and we can use that evidence to find $s$ with very high probability if we run the circuit sufficiently many times.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jawabannya ya, asalkan kita bersedia mengulangi prosesnya beberapa kali dan menerima bahwa itu bisa gagal dengan beberapa probabilitas, yang bisa kita buat sangat kecil dengan menjalankan sirkuit cukup banyak kali.\n"
"Ide dasarnya adalah bahwa setiap eksekusi sirkuit memberi kita bukti statistik tentang $s,$ dan kita bisa menggunakan bukti itu untuk menemukan $s$ dengan probabilitas sangat tinggi jika kita menjalankan sirkuit cukup banyak kali.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's suppose that we run the circuit independently $k$ times, for $k = n + 10.$\n"
"There's nothing special about this particular number of iterations — we could take $k$ to be larger (or smaller) depending on the probability of failure we're willing to tolerate, as we will see.\n"
"Choosing $k = n + 10$ will ensure that we have greater than a $99.9$% chance of recovering $s.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Misalkan kita menjalankan sirkuit secara independen $k$ kali, untuk $k = n + 10.$\n"
"Tidak ada yang istimewa tentang jumlah iterasi khusus ini — kita bisa mengambil $k$ lebih besar (atau lebih kecil) tergantung pada probabilitas kegagalan yang bersedia kita toleransi, seperti yang akan kita lihat.\n"
"Memilih $k = n + 10$ akan memastikan bahwa kita memiliki lebih dari $99.9$% kesempatan untuk memulihkan $s.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By running the circuit $k$ times, we obtain strings $y^1,...,y^{k} \\in \\Sigma^n.$\n"
"To be clear, the superscripts here are part of the names of these strings, not exponents or indexes to their bits, so we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan menjalankan sirkuit $k$ kali, kita mendapatkan string $y^1,...,y^{k} \\in \\Sigma^n.$\n"
"Untuk lebih jelasnya, superskrip di sini adalah bagian dari nama string-string ini, bukan eksponen atau indeks ke bit mereka, jadi kita memiliki\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"y^1 & = y^1_{n-1} \\cdots y^1_{0}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"y^2 & = y^2_{n-1} \\cdots y^2_{0}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& \\;\\; \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"y^{k} & = y^{k}_{n-1} \\cdots y^{k}_{0}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"y^1 & = y^1_{n-1} \\cdots y^1_{0}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"y^2 & = y^2_{n-1} \\cdots y^2_{0}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& \\;\\; \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"y^{k} & = y^{k}_{n-1} \\cdots y^{k}_{0}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now form a matrix $M$ having $k$ rows and $n$ columns by taking the bits "
"of these strings as binary-valued entries.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita sekarang membentuk matriks $M$ yang memiliki $k$ baris dan $n$ kolom "
"dengan mengambil bit-bit string ini sebagai entri bernilai biner.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
" y^1_{n-1} & \\cdots & y^1_{0}\\\\[1mm]\n"
" y^2_{n-1} & \\cdots & y^2_{0}\\\\[1mm]\n"
" \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots \\\\[1mm]\n"
" y^{k}_{n-1} & \\cdots & y^{k}_{0}\n"
" \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
" y^1_{n-1} & \\cdots & y^1_{0}\\\\[1mm]\n"
" y^2_{n-1} & \\cdots & y^2_{0}\\\\[1mm]\n"
" \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots \\\\[1mm]\n"
" y^{k}_{n-1} & \\cdots & y^{k}_{0}\n"
" \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, we don't know what $s$ is at this point — our goal is to find this string.\n"
"But imagine for a moment that we do know the string $s,$ and we form a column vector $v$ from the bits of the string $s = s_{n-1} \\cdots s_0$ as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang, kita tidak tahu apa $s$ pada titik ini — tujuan kita adalah menemukan string ini.\n"
"Tetapi bayangkan sebentar bahwa kita tahu string $s,$ dan kita membentuk vektor kolom $v$ dari bit-bit string $s = s_{n-1} \\cdots s_0$ sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"v = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"s_{n-1}\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"s_0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"v = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"s_{n-1}\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"s_0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we perform the matrix-vector multiplication $M v$ modulo $2$ — meaning "
"that we perform the multiplication as usual and then take the remainder of "
"the entries of the result after dividing by $2$ — we obtain the all-zero "
"vector.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika kita melakukan perkalian matriks-vektor $M v$ modulo $2$ — artinya kita"
" melakukan perkalian seperti biasa kemudian mengambil sisa entri hasilnya "
"setelah dibagi $2$ — kita mendapatkan vektor semua-nol.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M v = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"y^1 \\cdot s\\\\\n"
"y^2 \\cdot s\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"y^{k} \\cdot s\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0\\\\\n"
"0\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M v = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"y^1 \\cdot s\\\\\n"
"y^2 \\cdot s\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"y^{k} \\cdot s\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0\\\\\n"
"0\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, treated as a column vector $v$ as just described, the string $s$ will always be an element of the *null space* of the matrix $M,$ provided that we do the arithmetic modulo $2.$\n"
"This is true in both the case that $s = 0^n$ and $s\\neq 0^n.$\n"
"To be more precise, the all-zero vector is always in the null space of $M,$ and it's joined by the vector whose entries are the bits of $s$ in case $s\\neq 0^n.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Artinya, diperlakukan sebagai vektor kolom $v$ seperti yang baru saja dijelaskan, string $s$ akan selalu menjadi elemen dari *ruang nol* matriks $M,$ asalkan kita melakukan aritmetika modulo $2.$\n"
"Ini berlaku baik dalam kasus $s = 0^n$ maupun $s\\neq 0^n.$\n"
"Lebih tepatnya, vektor semua-nol selalu ada dalam ruang nol $M,$ dan bergabung dengan vektor yang entrinya adalah bit-bit $s$ dalam kasus $s\\neq 0^n.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The question remaining is whether there will be any other vectors in the null space of $M$ besides the ones corresponding to $0^n$ and $s.$\n"
"The answer is that this becomes increasingly unlikely as $k$ increases — and if we choose $k = n + 10,$ the null space of $M$ will contain no other vectors in addition to those corresponding to $0^n$ and $s$ with greater than a $99.9$% chance.\n"
"More generally, if we replace $k = n + 10$ with $k = n + r$ for an arbitrary choice of a positive integer $r,$ the probability that the vectors corresponding to $0^n$ and $s$ are alone in the null space of $M$ is at least $1 - 2^{-r}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertanyaan yang tersisa adalah apakah akan ada vektor lain dalam ruang nol $M$ selain yang bersesuaian dengan $0^n$ dan $s.$\n"
"Jawabannya adalah ini menjadi semakin tidak mungkin seiring $k$ meningkat — dan jika kita memilih $k = n + 10,$ ruang nol $M$ tidak akan berisi vektor lain selain yang bersesuaian dengan $0^n$ dan $s$ dengan lebih dari $99.9$% kesempatan.\n"
"Lebih umum, jika kita mengganti $k = n + 10$ dengan $k = n + r$ untuk pilihan bilangan bulat positif $r$ yang arbitrer, probabilitas bahwa vektor yang bersesuaian dengan $0^n$ dan $s$ sendirian dalam ruang nol $M$ adalah setidaknya $1 - 2^{-r}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using linear algebra, it is possible to efficiently calculate a description of the null space of $M$ modulo $2.$\n"
"Specifically, it can be done using *Gaussian elimination*, which works the same way when arithmetic is done modulo $2$ as it does with real or complex numbers.\n"
"So long as the vectors corresponding to $0^n$ and $s$ are alone in the null space of $M,$ which happens with high probability, we can deduce $s$ from the results of this computation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan aljabar linear, memungkinkan untuk secara efisien menghitung deskripsi ruang nol $M$ modulo $2.$\n"
"Secara khusus, ini bisa dilakukan menggunakan *eliminasi Gaussian*, yang bekerja dengan cara yang sama ketika aritmetika dilakukan modulo $2$ seperti halnya dengan bilangan nyata atau kompleks.\n"
"Selama vektor yang bersesuaian dengan $0^n$ dan $s$ sendirian dalam ruang nol $M,$ yang terjadi dengan probabilitas tinggi, kita dapat menyimpulkan $s$ dari hasil komputasi ini.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Classical difficulty {#classical-difficulty}"
msgstr "Kesulitan klasik {#classical-difficulty}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How many queries does a *classical* query algorithm need to solve Simon's problem?\n"
"The answer is: a lot, in general.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berapa banyak kueri yang diperlukan algoritma kueri *klasik* untuk memecahkan masalah Simon?\n"
"Jawabannya adalah: banyak, pada umumnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are different precise statements that can be made about the classical difficulty of this problem, and here's just one of them.\n"
"If we have any probabilistic query algorithm, and that algorithm makes fewer than $2^{n/2 - 1} - 1$ queries, which is a number of queries that's *exponential* in $n,$ then that algorithm will fail to solve Simon's problem with probability at least $1/2.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ada pernyataan yang berbeda dan tepat yang dapat dibuat tentang kesulitan klasik masalah ini, dan berikut adalah satu di antaranya.\n"
"Jika kita memiliki algoritma kueri probabilistik manapun, dan algoritma itu membuat kurang dari $2^{n/2 - 1} - 1$ kueri, yang merupakan jumlah kueri yang *eksponensial* dalam $n,$ maka algoritma itu akan gagal memecahkan masalah Simon dengan probabilitas setidaknya $1/2.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sometimes, proving impossibility results like this can be very challenging, but this one isn't too difficult to prove through an elementary probabilistic analysis.\n"
"Here, however, we'll only briefly examine the basic intuition behind it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kadang-kadang, membuktikan hasil impossibilitas seperti ini bisa sangat menantang, tetapi ini tidak terlalu sulit untuk dibuktikan melalui analisis probabilistik elementer.\n"
"Di sini, bagaimanapun, kita hanya akan secara singkat memeriksa intuisi dasar di baliknya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We're trying to find the hidden string $s,$ but so long as we don't query the function on two strings having the same output value, we'll get very limited information about $s.$\n"
"Intuitively speaking, all we'll learn is that the hidden string $s$ is *not* the exclusive-OR of any two distinct strings we've queried.\n"
"And if we query fewer than $2^{n/2 - 1} - 1$ strings, then there will still be a lot of choices for $s$ that we haven't ruled out because there aren't enough pairs of strings to do this.\n"
"This isn't a formal proof, it's just the basic idea.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita mencoba menemukan string tersembunyi $s,$ tetapi selama kita tidak melakukan kueri ke fungsi pada dua string yang memiliki nilai keluaran yang sama, kita akan mendapatkan informasi yang sangat terbatas tentang $s.$\n"
"Secara intuitif, yang akan kita pelajari hanyalah bahwa string tersembunyi $s$ *bukan* XOR eksklusif dari dua string berbeda yang telah kita kueri.\n"
"Dan jika kita melakukan kueri kurang dari $2^{n/2 - 1} - 1$ string, masih akan ada banyak pilihan untuk $s$ yang belum kita singkirkan karena tidak ada cukup pasang string untuk melakukannya.\n"
"Ini bukan bukti formal, ini hanya ide dasarnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, in summary, Simon's algorithm provides us with a striking advantage of quantum over classical algorithms within the query model.\n"
"In particular, Simon's algorithm solves Simon's problem with a number of queries that's *linear* in the number of input bits $n$ of our function, whereas any classical algorithm, even if it's probabilistic, needs to make a number of queries that's *exponential* in $n$ in order to solve Simon's problem with a reasonable probability of success.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi, singkatnya, algoritma Simon memberikan kita keunggulan yang mencolok dari kuantum atas algoritma klasik dalam model kueri.\n"
"Khususnya, algoritma Simon memecahkan masalah Simon dengan jumlah kueri yang *linear* dalam jumlah bit masukan $n$ dari fungsi kita, sedangkan algoritma klasik manapun, bahkan jika itu probabilistik, perlu membuat jumlah kueri yang *eksponensial* dalam $n$ untuk memecahkan masalah Simon dengan probabilitas keberhasilan yang wajar.\n"
